# Storybook 10.6.1 declares an **optional** peer on `vite-plus` that only reaches
# ^0.1.15 || ^0.2.0, while this toolchain is Vite+ 1.x. `10.6.1` is Storybook's latest
# release, so there is no version to upgrade to that accepts it, and pinning Vite+ back to
# 0.2.x would give up the toolchain this repo now runs on.
#
# npm resolves that conflict to a hard `ERESOLVE` error on a clean install — which is what
# CI's `vp install` hit, killing all three jobs in their setup step — while a developer
# machine with an existing node_modules only ever saw a warning, so it looked like a CI bug.
#
# The peer is optional and unused: Storybook falls back to its own Vite when `vite-plus` is
# not satisfying, which is exactly what it was doing before this migration. Measured both
# ways on a clean tree: without this file `npm install` exits `ERESOLVE`; with it, 372
# packages install. Remove it when Storybook's range catches up with Vite+ 1.x.
legacy-peer-deps=true
